Alembic migrations for the dashcam analyser.

The application runs `alembic upgrade head` itself at startup (app.db.session.init_db),
so a fresh /data volume needs no manual step.

Manual use, from the `backend/` directory:

    alembic upgrade head
    alembic downgrade -1
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
    alembic upgrade head --sql          # offline: emit SQL instead of applying it

The database URL is never read from alembic.ini. env.py takes it from
app.config.get_config().sync_sqlalchemy_url so migrations can never target a different
database than the running application. Set DASHCAM_DATA_DIR (or DASHCAM_DATABASE_URL) to
point them elsewhere.

SQLite cannot ALTER most things in place, so env.py enables render_as_batch: schema
changes are emitted as create-copy-drop-rename. Write new migrations with
`with op.batch_alter_table(...) as batch_op:` when altering existing columns.
